{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"bcf9f07b-7005-4a70-a560-f123d370719b","agentId":"a6ebff88f4151f3df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes, no searching, no screenshots. Report under 70 words. Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. Files: cuore/services/flow_bridge.py, mes-log-mcp/mes/shop.py, cuore/services/jobs_bridge.py, cuore/services/shop_bridge.py, cuore/tests/check_flow.py (+2 checks). Do not edit templates.\n\nMechanic review findings to fix:\n1. Contradiction on one screen: the hero shows \"4 open codes\" and verdict UNVERIFIED_REPAIR from the MES corpus, while flow step 3 says \"no codes read yet; verdict not computed\" and step 4 says \"no MES log since intake\", because flow_bridge only counts evidence dated after intake. Rule: evidence that exists before intake still counts, labelled with its date: step 4 is done when the corpus has any session/scan for the VIN (why: \"codes from MES logs, newest 4 Oct; read the car again to refresh\"), step 3 is done whenever build_view yields a verdict other than NO_DATA (why = the verdict sentence). Post-intake reads upgrade the why text. Never show \"verdict not computed\" when a verdict exists.\n2. \"(unnamed vehicle)\": when a visit/job is created from /start with no name, resolve the vehicle name from mes_bridge.workup(vin)[\"identity\"][\"vehicle\"] (or mes vehicles list), else decode the WMI (ZASF -> \"Alfa Romeo\", ZN6/ZN7 -> \"Maserati\") with the model UNKNOWN; store it on the visit and job and expose it wherever `vehicle`/`bar.name` is built from the visit (shop_bridge/jobs_bridge). Never emit \"(unnamed vehicle)\" when a VIN is known.\nChecks: after intake for VIN ZASFAKPN5J7B88115 the flow's step 3 and 4 are done with a why naming the verdict/date; the visit's vehicle name contains \"Stelvio\". Run check_flow.py, cuore/tests/check_shop_page.py, check_jobs_page.py."},"uuid":"c1349e96-d883-44f2-9989-5cb2acfcec46","timestamp":"2026-10-08T14:32:53.428Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
