{"parentUuid":"1ff4b002-9bb5-4de0-b93e-a9e7547c3572","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6ebff88f4151f3df","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfpwjPaKF517kFvyKidw1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VLRpmHjgVb4343HW1bipAG","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Both findings fixed, no templates touched.\n\n1. flow_bridge.py: step 4 now done whenever the corpus has any session/scan for the VIN (not just post-intake), why = \"codes from MES logs, newest {date}; read the car again to refresh\" when pre-intake, or \"codes read since intake\" when fresh. Step 3 decoupled from step 4: done whenever dossier_bridge.build_view's verdict.state != NO_DATA, why = the verdict's own summary sentence. Never shows \"verdict not computed\" once a real verdict exists.\n\n2. Vehicle-name resolution: shop_bridge.py gained resolve_vehicle_name(vin) (corpus vehicle list -> mes_bridge.workup identity.vehicle -> WMI decode ZASF->Alfa Romeo / ZN6,ZN7->Maserati with model \"UNKNOWN\" -> VIN itself), used by intake(). mes/shop.py's intake() independently falls back to its own WMI decode when called with no vehicle (defense in depth for direct mes.shop callers). jobs_bridge.py now exposes a \"vehicle\" key in build_job_view, read from the current visit (mes.shop) or shop_bridge.resolve_vehicle_name. \"(unnamed vehicle)\" can no longer occur once a VIN is known.\n\nAdded 2 checks to check_flow.py (check 6) against real VIN ZASFAKPN5J7B88115: step 3/4 are \"done\" with why naming the verdict/date, and the visit's vehicle name contains \"Stelvio\". Had to adjust pre-existing check 3 (VIN_3, fictional/no real corpus) to mock dossier_bridge.build_view with an UNVERIFIED_REPAIR verdict, since under the corrected rule a fictional VIN with no real logs now correctly stays NO_DATA/step-3-undone — that's the bug fix working as intended, not a regression.\n\nResults: check_flow.py 15/15, check_shop_page.py 19/19, check_jobs_page.py 24/24 — all pass.\n\nFiles touched: C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\flow_bridge.py, C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\shop_bridge.py, C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\jobs_bridge.py, C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\shop.py, C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_flow.py."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_read_input_tokens":147543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":540,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VLRpmHjgVb4343HW1bipAG":{"message":"Both findings fixed, no templates touched.\n\n1. flow_bridge.py: step 4 now done whenever the corpus has any session/scan for the VIN (not just post-intake), why = \"codes from MES logs, newest {date}; read the car again to refresh\" when pre-intake, or \"codes read since intake\" when fresh. Step 3 decoupled from step 4: done whenever dossier_bridge.build_view's verdict.state != NO_DATA, why = the verdict's own summary sentence. Never shows \"verdict not computed\" once a real verdict exists.\n\n2. Vehicle-name resolution: shop_bridge.py gained resolve_vehicle_name(vin) (corpus vehicle list -> mes_bridge.workup identity.vehicle -> WMI decode ZASF->Alfa Romeo / ZN6,ZN7->Maserati with model \"UNKNOWN\" -> VIN itself), used by intake(). mes/shop.py's intake() independently falls back to its own WMI decode when called with no vehicle (defense in depth for direct mes.shop callers). jobs_bridge.py now exposes a \"vehicle\" key in build_job_view, read from the current visit (mes.shop) or shop_bridge.resolve_vehicle_name. \"(unnamed vehicle)\" can no longer occur once a VIN is known.\n\nAdded 2 checks to check_flow.py (check 6) against real VIN ZASFAKPN5J7B88115: step 3/4 are \"done\" with why naming the verdict/date, and the visit's vehicle name contains \"Stelvio\". Had to adjust pre-existing check 3 (VIN_3, fictional/no real corpus) to mock dossier_bridge.build_view with an UNVERIFIED_REPAIR verdict, since under the corrected rule a fictional VIN with no real logs now correctly stays NO_DATA/step-3-undone — that's the bug fix working as intended, not a regression.\n\nResults: check_flow.py 15/15, check_shop_page.py 19/19, check_jobs_page.py 24/24 — all pass.\n\nFiles touched: C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\flow_bridge.py, C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\shop_bridge.py, C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\jobs_bridge.py, C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\shop.py, C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_flow.py."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"beac66c4-2fd5-47e2-91a7-250148cd89cb","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfpwjPBG3Drnk66qFrYBi","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"38c9d1eb-fdfe-40bd-91bd-ac6a2417cf3d","timestamp":"2026-10-08T14:41:15.917Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
